"` to mute it."],[414,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[508,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1465,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1473,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[913,"`Enter/Space`"],[456,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[681,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[423,"`Escape`"],[839,"`Escape`"],[915,"`Escape`"],[1667,"`Escape`"],[493,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1992,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[595,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1950,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[510,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[669,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[698,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1865,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[511,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[1920,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[728,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1919,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[763,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[151,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[383,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[832,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[827,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1000,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1717,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1433,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1657,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[689,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[672,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[907,"`Popov