` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[427,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[594,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[593,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[347,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[963,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1065,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1190,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1064,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1189,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1619,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1618,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[769,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1464,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1539,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[875,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1504,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[395,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[833,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[509,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[1918,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1246,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[46,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1350,"`Space` to